tourHistory:
  - >-
    After four years on "indefinite hiatus" following their bitter 2005 split,
    Mark Hoppus, Tom DeLonge, and Travis Barker reconciled in the wake of
    Barker’s survival of the September 2008 plane crash and longtime producer
    Jerry Finn’s death. Announcing their return at the February 2009 Grammys,
    they mounted a triumphant North American amphitheater run with Weezer and
    Taking Back Sunday in tow.
  - >-
    This Kansas City-area stop doubled as a mini-festival, adding hometown
    favorites Mac Lethal and The Republic Tigers alongside Star Trak duo Chester
    French and Billy Boy on Poison.
